  "verbalization": "Isosakuranetin 7-O-rutinoside appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a multi-step mechanism involving a series of enzymatic targets. The drug is first shown to target the 2-hydroxychromene-2-carboxylate isomerase, which in turn is a target of 25-Anhydroalisol A and Meliatoosenin M. Both of these compounds are linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a potential pathway where Isosakuranetin 7-O-rutinoside may modulate the activity of these enzymes, ultimately influencing the complex. Additionally, the drug is also shown to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is a target of 2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-(3,3-Dimethylallyl)Acetophenone, which also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This suggests that the drug may exert its effects through multiple pathways, potentially involving different enzymes that ultimately converge on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Isosakuranetin 7-O-rutinoside and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
